# `kevin logs`

Prints the output of a step. With no step name, it prints the output of every step, in order. It works while `kevin run` is running and after it exits, including after a crash.

```sh
kevin logs
kevin logs web
kevin logs web --follow
```

[[template "flags" .]]

See [`kevin status`]({{< relref "/docs/reference/commands/status" >}})
for step state, and [`kevin run`]({{< relref "/docs/reference/commands/run" >}})'s
`--detach`/`-d` flag.
